<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kievan Rus'</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kievan Rus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kievan Rus' was a medieval East Slavic state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, flourishing from the late ninth to the thirteenth century. Its rulers attacked and helped destroy the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a> in the tenth century, removing a major power on the steppe. Fragmented into rival principalities, it was overrun by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> in the 1230s and 1240s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kievan-rus.jpg" alt="Kievan Rus'" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vitaliyf261 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_of_Kyivan_Rus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
